# Specific Task Bypass Configuration

If the user starts a prompt with the prefix "[AUTO-PILOT]", you are authorized to act as an autonomous agent.

- Do not stop to prompt for file modification permissions.
- Proceed through multi-step edits sequentially until the goal is achieved.
- If a command or tool requires execution, consider it pre-approved under the scope of the stated task (e.g. `npm run build`, `npm install`, `npx tsc`, preview/serve scripts, and image/asset processing for this repo).
- Still respect git safety: never force-push, never amend pushed commits, never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- Still verify the build and static preview before resting (see `.cursor/rules/verify-build-before-resting.mdc`).
- If you hit a genuinely destructive or irreversible action (deleting large amounts of untracked work, history rewrites, anything outside the stated goal), pause and confirm.

When the prefix is absent, behave normally and ask before risky or ambiguous actions.

## Note on scope

This rule reminds the model of the maintainer's intent; it does not by itself change Cursor's approval UI. To make commands auto-run without clicking "Allow," also enable the less-restrictive / auto-run options in Cursor Settings (search `auto run`, `approve`, or `sandbox`).
